352	5	7	Endpoint configuration and subscription confirmation.\n\nRemediation\n\nUpdate IAM policy to allow sns:Publish/lambda:InvokeFunction.\n\nRe-subscribe or manually confirm subscription.\n\nPost-mortem\n\nAdd subscription health checks and alerting.\n\n6. Lambda and EMR/Glue trigger failure\n\nSymptoms\n\nLambda logs show failure to start Glue/EMR job.\n\nImmediate checks\n\nValidate Glue job ARN or EMR cluster ID.\n\nCheck IAM role used by Lambda.\n\nRemediation\n\nCorrect ARNs, update IAM role permissions, ensure cluster exists.\n\nPost-mortem\n\nAdd integration tests for trigger flows.\n\n7. File size too high for EMR/Glue\n\nSymptoms\n\nOutOfMemoryError, job timeouts, or long runtimes.\n\nImmediate checks\n\nCheck file size in S3 and job memory metrics.\n\nRemediation\n\nPartition or chunk large files.\n\nIncrease cluster resources or worker memory.\n\nUse streaming processing where possible.\n\nPost-mortem\n\nAdd file size thresholds and pre-processing to split large files.\n\n\n\n8. Athena table not queryable\n\nSymptoms	[0.01794821,-0.07652637,-0.011109393,-0.06496034,0.0384569,0.012199909,-0.03777683,-0.012878404,-0.0149992835,0.059337042,-0.0066023762,0.1037555,0.0233588,0.07762988,-0.06643999,0.0046074563,-0.033831652,0.02470421,-0.052236255,-0.024791943,0.013888774,0.04174767,0.012312413,-0.02943978,0.012374988,0.041893274,-0.03074595,0.026449436,0.016647805,0.005358865,-0.048899196,-0.07028019,-0.014165746,0.0005266668,1.6661417e-06,-0.0433148,0.021902278,0.007821927,0.006600578,0.022627138,0.009597712,-0.10248913,0.0026352308,0.03726783,-0.015313084,0.014657355,-0.048887655,-0.0055018105,0.062710375,0.021505265,-0.016604131,0.01673248,0.022510774,-0.021278165,-0.044618968,-0.047429394,0.008172845,-0.019258374,0.044897795,-0.04858843,0.0019301197,-0.018187223,0.030184995,0.023066066,-0.0015739403,0.05485234,-0.037597414,-0.041892603,0.042849623,-0.06553083,0.085812576,-0.01681084,-0.021380957,-0.014473535,-0.040764887,0.022483725,0.019409781,-0.0094