357	5	12	If unresolved within SLA, escalate to L2.\n\nTroubleshooting and Diagnostics\n\nCommon diagnostic commands\n\nCheck Docker containers:\n\nbash\n\ndocker ps\n\ndocker logs pgvector-local\n\nConnect to Postgres inside container:\n\nbash\n\ndocker exec -it pgvector-local psql -U postgres -d kb_db\n\nConnect from host:\n\nbash\n\npsql -h localhost -U postgres -d kb_db -W\n\nCheck Glue catalog partitions (example CLI):\n\nbash\n\naws glue get-table --database-name mydb --name mytable\n\nRepair Athena partitions:\n\nsql\n\nMSCK REPAIR TABLE my_table;\n\nWhen connection refused\n\nVerify port mapping and that no local Postgres is conflicting. Consider remapping to 5433:5432.\n\n\n\nWhen authentication fails\n\nRecreate volume and container to apply new POSTGRES_PASSWORD:\n\nbash\n\ndocker compose down -v\n\ndocker compose up -d\n\nSecurity, Access Control, and Compliance\n\nDatabase access\n\nUse least privilege for DB users. Create separate read/write roles for agents and admins.\n\nRotate DB credentials periodically.\n\nIAM and AWS	[-0.010287326,0.041913714,0.011909254,-0.004098416,0.05640931,0.021415817,0.011257236,0.009430532,0.02058664,0.029068809,0.012999158,0.00182122,0.033621497,0.05490361,-0.005825782,0.046551403,0.018885657,0.0049549676,-0.07181816,-0.03570697,0.01613851,0.0041343314,0.0056086928,-0.03408809,0.014781832,0.031803347,0.01878789,-0.044685356,-0.038346212,0.047285184,-0.042386916,-0.005436896,-0.052343104,0.03857612,1.8781935e-06,0.00033791517,-0.0066919127,-0.013555785,0.040821448,-0.030611552,0.004045221,-0.097790316,0.030867843,-0.007179087,-0.051822856,-0.06294526,-0.0063152276,0.028478125,0.07424848,-0.03425348,0.0013577259,0.057240188,0.032997515,-0.018486355,-7.152319e-05,-0.09913632,-0.029968271,0.0013856438,0.003095816,-0.06641558,0.04435784,0.021085154,-0.0043926933,-0.013613818,-0.02686031,0.056137703,0.042541843,-0.009515462,-0.006379662,-0.039051425,0.06855075,-0.035195734,-0.05383465,0.030274095,0.005569522,0.01892201,0.0044727