358	5	13	Rotate DB credentials periodically.\n\nIAM and AWS\n\nUse fine-grained IAM roles for Lambda, Glue, and EMR.\n\nEnsure S3 bucket policies restrict access to required principals.\n\nData protection\n\nEncrypt S3 at rest (SSE-S3 or SSE-KMS).\n\nUse SSL/TLS for DB connections where applicable.\n\nAudit and logging\n\nEnable CloudTrail for AWS API auditing.\n\nKeep audit logs for at least 90 days (adjust per compliance).\n\nMaintenance, Backups, and Disaster Recovery\n\nDatabase backups\n\nFor Docker local dev: periodically pg_dump the DB:\n\nbash\n\npg_dump -h localhost -U postgres -d kb_db -F c -f backups/kb_db_$(date +%F).dump\n\nFor production: use managed DB snapshots or scheduled backups.\n\nRestore\n\nbash\n\npg_restore -h localhost -U postgres -d kb_db -v backups/kb_db_2026-08-23.dump\n\nGlue/EMR\n\nKeep job definitions in version control.\n\nUse automated deployment for job scripts and bootstrap actions.\n\nDisaster recovery\n\n\n\nDocument RTO/RPO.\n\nKeep offsite backups of DB dumps and critical config files.	[-0.0057447804,0.036057435,0.007880515,-0.0028312735,-0.024063988,0.021149576,-0.0103440825,-0.029063521,-0.010423258,0.0036801626,0.027175173,0.020670792,0.00846381,0.08278571,0.016911259,-0.022152498,-0.016781734,0.008978035,-0.076999314,0.015020673,0.007971206,-0.0019492584,0.0024262113,-0.016135698,0.022024877,0.01908655,0.0023457615,0.021599866,0.014116735,0.019541277,-0.049857058,0.0085510975,-0.039746214,0.0044601187,1.5138152e-06,0.011783554,-0.06592591,-0.019933313,0.012673513,-0.045954823,-0.0034342299,-0.075134575,0.023432529,0.008251198,-0.009725888,-0.041896924,0.028909698,0.031136293,0.067677476,-0.012971788,0.0010447762,-0.001759032,-0.00085914857,0.024647748,-0.027737573,-0.02980823,-0.022569973,0.007745067,0.012367028,-0.0067069586,0.040718056,-0.016356545,-0.007076317,-0.0050280048,0.038135093,0.016625123,0.03928062,-0.014505477,-0.038531747,-0.04441017,0.065922484,-0.063311696,-0.0019808852,0.024408322,-0.0012869249,-0.02637518