329	2	9	IAM Best Practices\n\nUse least privilege for Lambda, Glue, and EMR roles.\n\nSeparate roles for read only and write operations to S3 and Glue.\n\nUse resource policies for cross account access.\n\nData Protection\n\nEncrypt S3 buckets with SSE KMS.\n\nUse TLS for all service endpoints.\n\nRotate credentials and use secrets manager for DB passwords.\n\nKB Access\n\nCreate DB roles for agents and human operators with least privilege.\n\nUse SSL for Postgres connections where possible.\n\nTesting and Validation\n\nUnit Tests\n\nTest parsing logic for each upstream file format.\n\nTest Lambda validation logic with positive and negative cases.\n\nIntegration Tests\n\nSimulate file arrival in staging S3 and validate end to end flow through Glue/EMR to Athena and Snowflake.\n\nValidate agent behavior by injecting synthetic errors and verifying RCA generation and validation.\n\nPerformance Tests\n\nLoad test Glue/EMR jobs with large files and measure scaling behavior.	[0.02590691,-0.049579263,-0.0070524705,-0.024802532,0.0046441783,-0.0075925123,0.04753292,-0.034903906,-0.005003055,0.025807103,-0.009310983,0.024381964,0.020457888,0.09987887,-0.009253625,0.00938454,0.03975602,0.0045546824,-0.051624127,-0.01744661,2.480032e-05,0.0025198476,0.02441084,-0.037399948,0.011016429,0.047049176,-0.048424862,0.08340194,-0.018404277,-0.014085453,-0.050190117,-0.013759438,-0.021646943,0.042274162,1.5957456e-06,-0.037966155,-0.027302315,-0.016042862,-0.025304168,0.01884248,0.056824267,-0.009340808,0.019308371,0.039172284,-0.01744391,0.007472347,0.007919379,-0.0034134397,0.077942595,0.021969464,-0.011341516,0.019876424,-0.041276652,-0.018591639,-0.038351234,-0.002744467,0.0001283066,0.01496569,0.04491382,0.018674972,0.02359841,-0.034152754,0.026468921,0.032184247,0.05551265,0.042847876,0.004253193,-0.036172774,-0.059029996,-0.06816471,0.084137954,-0.01191612,-0.04806008,0.0033131794,-0.016344657,0.0031332355,0.03301908,0.0065477765,0.06535254,-0.019202875,-0.0150084635,0.01369845